# ABP Development Workflow

> **Tutorials**: https://abp.io/docs/latest/tutorials

CoachApp is a **single-app**, feature-folder solution. Add a feature as a **vertical slice**,
bottom-up, mirroring the reference `Trainee` / `TrainingPlan` slices. Namespaces are
feature-based (`CoachApp.Entites.<Feature>`, `CoachApp.Apis.<Feature>`, `CoachApp.Enums`,
`CoachApp.Permissions`, `CoachApp.EntityConfigurations.<Feature>`). `<Feature>` is the
pluralized entity.

## Adding a New Entity (Full Flow)

### 1. Domain.Shared — consts, enum, error codes
```csharp
// Entites/Trainees/TraineeConsts.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Entites.Trainees)
// Single source of length truth — reused by entity, DTO and EF config.
public static class TraineeConsts
{
    public const int MaxCodeLength = 32;
    public const int MaxFirstNameLength = 64;
    public const int MaxLastNameLength = 64;
}

// Enums/Gender.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Enums) — byte-backed, explicit values
public enum Gender : byte { Unspecified = 0, Male = 1, Female = 2 }

// CoachAppDomainErrorCodes.cs — one code per business rule (mapped to a localization key)
public const string TraineeCodeAlreadyExists = "CoachApp:00001";
```

### 2. Domain — entity with `static Create`
Pragmatic domain model: `FullAuditedAggregateRoot<Guid>` (`+ IMultiTenant` when tenant-scoped),
**public settable properties** for plain fields, a `protected` ctor for the ORM, and a
`static Create(...)` factory that validates required fields/lengths. Guard a real invariant (one
that needs no I/O) with a behavior method that throws and keep its fields `protected set`.

```csharp
// Entites/Trainees/Trainee.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Entites.Trainees)
public class Trainee : FullAuditedAggregateRoot<Guid>, IMultiTenant
{
    public virtual Guid? TenantId { get; set; }
    public virtual string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public virtual string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public virtual Gender Gender { get; set; }
    public virtual bool IsActive { get; set; }

    protected Trainee() { } // For ORM

    public static Trainee Create(Guid id, string code, string firstName,
        Gender gender = Gender.Unspecified, Guid? tenantId = null)
    {
        return new Trainee
        {
            Id = id,
            Code = Check.NotNullOrWhiteSpace(code, nameof(code), TraineeConsts.MaxCodeLength),
            FirstName = Check.NotNullOrWhiteSpace(firstName, nameof(firstName), TraineeConsts.MaxFirstNameLength),
            Gender = gender,
            TenantId = tenantId,
            IsActive = true
        };
    }
}
```
> **Do NOT** add a separate `*Factory` class, and **do NOT** add a `*Manager` for simple CRUD.
> Add a `*Manager : DomainService` only for a genuine cross-aggregate domain rule.

### 3. Application.Contracts — DTOs + service interface
```csharp
// Entites/Trainees/TraineeDto.cs
public class TraineeDto : FullAuditedEntityDto<Guid>
{
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public Gender Gender { get; set; }
    public bool IsActive { get; set; }
}

// Entites/Trainees/CreateUpdateTraineeDto.cs — DataAnnotations validation (lengths from Consts)
public class CreateUpdateTraineeDto
{
    [Required, StringLength(TraineeConsts.MaxCodeLength)]
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, StringLength(TraineeConsts.MaxFirstNameLength)]
    public string FirstName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public Gender Gender { get; set; } = Gender.Unspecified;
    public bool IsActive { get; set; } = true;
}

// Entites/Trainees/GetTraineeListInput.cs
public class GetTraineeListInput : PagedAndSortedResultRequestDto
{
    public string? Filter { get; set; }
    public bool? IsActive { get; set; }
}

// Entites/Trainees/ITraineeAppService.cs — Id passed separately from the update DTO
public interface ITraineeAppService : IApplicationService
{
    Task<TraineeDto> GetAsync(Guid id);
    Task<PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>> GetListAsync(GetTraineeListInput input);
    Task<TraineeDto> CreateAsync(CreateUpdateTraineeDto input);
    Task<TraineeDto> UpdateAsync(Guid id, CreateUpdateTraineeDto input);
    Task DeleteAsync(Guid id);
}
```

### 4. Application.Contracts — permissions
```csharp
// Permissions/CoachAppPermissions.cs
public static class Trainees
{
    public const string Default = GroupName + ".Trainees";
    public const string Create = Default + ".Create";
    public const string Update = Default + ".Update";
    public const string Delete = Default + ".Delete";
}
// Register the children in CoachAppPermissionDefinitionProvider.Define(...).
```

### 5. Application — fat AppService + Mapster line
Inject the **generic `IRepository<T, Guid>`** and do querying inline; run cross-aggregate checks
here. Map out with `ObjectMapper` (Mapster).

```csharp
// Apis/Trainees/TraineeAppService.cs  (namespace CoachApp.Apis.Trainees)
[Authorize(CoachAppPermissions.Trainees.Default)]
public class TraineeAppService : CoachAppAppService, ITraineeAppService
{
    private readonly IRepository<Trainee, Guid> _traineeRepository;

    public TraineeAppService(IRepository<Trainee, Guid> traineeRepository)
        => _traineeRepository = traineeRepository;

    public virtual async Task<PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>> GetListAsync(GetTraineeListInput input)
    {
        var query = await _traineeRepository.GetQueryableAsync();
        query = query
            .WhereIf(!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input.Filter), x => x.Code.Contains(input.Filter!))
            .WhereIf(input.IsActive.HasValue, x => x.IsActive == input.IsActive!.Value);

        var totalCount = await AsyncExecuter.CountAsync(query);
        var sorting = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input.Sorting) ? $"{nameof(Trainee.Code)} asc" : input.Sorting;
        var trainees = await AsyncExecuter.ToListAsync(
            query.OrderBy(sorting).Skip(input.SkipCount).Take(input.MaxResultCount)); // System.Linq.Dynamic.Core

        return new PagedResultDto<TraineeDto>(
            totalCount, ObjectMapper.Map<List<Trainee>, List<TraineeDto>>(trainees));
    }

    [Authorize(CoachAppPermissions.Trainees.Create)]
    public virtual async Task<TraineeDto> CreateAsync(CreateUpdateTraineeDto input)
    {
        await CheckCodeDuplicationAsync(input.Code); // cross-aggregate uniqueness — needs the repo
        var trainee = Trainee.Create(GuidGenerator.Create(), input.Code, input.FirstName, input.Gender, CurrentTenant.Id);
        await _traineeRepository.InsertAsync(trainee, autoSave: true);
        return ObjectMapper.Map<Trainee, TraineeDto>(trainee);
    }
}
```

**Mapster mapping** — add one line to `CoachAppMapsterConfig.Configure()` (entity → DTO only):
```csharp
TypeAdapterConfig<Trainee, TraineeDto>.NewConfig();
```
Do NOT use Mapperly (`[Mapper]`/`MapperBase`) or AutoMapper (`CreateMap`/`Profile`). Use
`.Ignore(...)` / `.Map(dest => ..., src => ...)` for properties the service fills or shape
mismatches. Mapping always goes through `ObjectMapper.Map<...>()`.

### 6. EntityFrameworkCore — EF configuration + DbSet
```csharp
// EntityConfigurations/Trainees/TraineeConfiguration.cs  (namespace CoachApp.EntityConfigurations.Trainees)
public class TraineeConfiguration : IEntityTypeConfiguration<Trainee>
{
    public void Configure(EntityTypeBuilder<Trainee> b)
    {
        b.ToTable(CoachAppConsts.DbTablePrefix + "Trainees", CoachAppConsts.DbSchema);
        b.ConfigureByConvention();
        b.Property(x => x.Code).IsRequired().HasMaxLength(TraineeConsts.MaxCodeLength);
        b.Property(x => x.FirstName).IsRequired().HasMaxLength(TraineeConsts.MaxFirstNameLength);
        b.Property(x => x.Gender).HasConversion<byte>();
        b.HasIndex(x => new { x.TenantId, x.Code });
    }
}
// Auto-applied by builder.ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly(...) in CoachAppDbContext.

// CoachAppDbContext.cs — add one DbSet per aggregate on the single DbContext
public DbSet<Trainee> Trainees { get; set; }
```
> There is **no per-module DbContext** and no hand-called configuration extension — just add the
> `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` class and the `DbSet<T>`.

### 7. Localization
Add keys to **both** `Domain.Shared/Localization/CoachApp/en.json` and `ar.json`:
```json
{
  "Permission:Trainees": "Trainees",
  "Permission:Trainees.Create": "Create trainee",
  "CoachApp:00001": "A trainee with code {Code} already exists.",
  "Code": "Code",
  "FirstName": "First name"
}
```

### 8. Migration (write freely — ASK before applying)
```bash
dotnet ef migrations add Added_Trainee \
  --project src/CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore \
  --startup-project src/CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore

# Apply ONLY with the user's approval (also seeds admin/permissions):
dotnet run --project src/CoachApp.DbMigrator
# or EF-only:  dotnet ef database update
```
Review the generated migration before it is applied (watch for accidental table renames if a
namespace moved). **Writing the migration file is fine; applying it to the database needs the
user's OK.**

### 9. Tests (when asked)
Mirror `test/CoachApp.Application.Tests`; cover the happy path + each `BusinessException` +
authorization.
```csharp
public class TraineeAppService_Tests : CoachAppApplicationTestBase
{
    private readonly ITraineeAppService _traineeAppService;

    public TraineeAppService_Tests()
        => _traineeAppService = GetRequiredService<ITraineeAppService>();

    [Fact]
    public async Task Should_Create_Trainee()
    {
        var result = await _traineeAppService.CreateAsync(new CreateUpdateTraineeDto
        {
            Code = "T-001",
            FirstName = "Alex"
        });

        result.Id.ShouldNotBe(Guid.Empty);
        result.Code.ShouldBe("T-001");
    }
}
```

## Modifying an existing entity
Touch the SAME files in sync: `Consts` → entity prop / behavior / invariant → DTO(s) + annotations
→ `CoachAppMapsterConfig` (only if a new mapping is needed) → `EntityConfigurations/<Feature>`
block → `DbSet` (only for a brand-new entity) → localization → migration. Never change an entity
property without also updating the DTO, EF config and `Consts`.

## Quick Reference Commands

### Build Solution
```bash
dotnet build CoachApp.slnx
```

### Run Migrations
```bash
dotnet ef migrations add MigrationName \
  --project src/CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore --startup-project src/CoachApp.EntityFrameworkCore
dotnet run --project src/CoachApp.DbMigrator   # apply migration + seed data (ASK FIRST)
```

### Run / smoke-test
```bash
dotnet run --project src/CoachApp.HttpApi.Host   # Swagger to try endpoints
```

## Checklist for New Features

- [ ] Consts + enum + error code in Domain.Shared
- [ ] Entity in Domain with `static Create` (public setters; invariant behavior methods; no Factory/Manager)
- [ ] DTOs (`TraineeDto`, `CreateUpdateTraineeDto`, `GetTraineeListInput`) + `I<Entity>AppService` in Application.Contracts
- [ ] Permissions defined + registered in the provider
- [ ] Fat AppService in Application (generic repo, inline querying, cross-aggregate checks, `[Authorize]`)
- [ ] Mapster line added to `CoachAppMapsterConfig` (entity → DTO)
- [ ] `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` + `DbSet<T>` on the single `CoachAppDbContext`
- [ ] Localization keys added (en + ar)
- [ ] Migration generated (applied only with approval)
- [ ] Tests written (when asked)
